TI  - Golpes mediáticos y desinformación en la era digital. La guerra irregular en América Latina
AU  - Sierra Caballero, Francisco
AU  - Sola-Morales, Salomé
T2  - Comunicación y sociedad
AB  - Abstract This article reflects on the role of the media and social networks in the phenomenon of “media coups” in Latin America. To this end, the propaganda model is explored through the analysis of four relevant cases of manipulation and disinformation in the region: those of Venezuela, Mexico, Brazil and Ecuador. The main conclusion reached is that it is necessary to regulate the traditional and digital media system for democracy and peace to prevent disinformation and “media coups”.
