TI  - Racionalidad neoliberal y migración: Marco de Gobernanza para las Migraciones de la OIM y Programa Especial de Migración
AU  - Ortiz Gómez, María Guadalupe
T2  - Si Somos Americanos
AB  - Abstract: This article presents an analysis of the Migration Governance Framework (MGM) of the International Organization for Migration (IOM) and the Special Migration Program (PEM) of the government of Mexico in the period from 2014 to 2018. The objective of determining, firstly, what is the underlying political rationality in the speeches of these programs; second, reflect on the affinities that exist between the MGM and the PEM; and third, analyze the implications that the application of that political rationality has on the human dimension of the migration phenomenon. The evidence showed that the MGM discourse is based on neoliberal political rationality. It is proposed that good governance of migration is one that focuses on generating development processes by converting migrants into agents of development, which is why they are classified into two categories: desired migrants and unwanted migrants. This classification objectifies people, which contradicts the human rights framework.
